cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "O*NET Task→Ability Mapping Dataset"
abstract: >-
  A task-level mapping from 18,796 O*NET work tasks, spanning all 23 SOC major
  groups, to the 52 O*NET human abilities each task requires, with a graded
  importance weight per (task, ability) pair. The dataset contains 95,330
  task-to-ability mappings. Labels were generated with a large language model
  against the O*NET taxonomy using one consistent method across all groups, then
  validated: three independent annotators each re-reviewed a 200-task audit
  sample and endorsed 98.9% of the model-proposed abilities. Built as the
  empirical foundation for the ATES (Agentic Task Exposure Score) framework, it
  also stands alone for research on skill demand, automation exposure, and the
  division of tasks between people and AI.
